    "summary": "Docker containers and virtual machines both isolate workloads but differ fundamentally: containers share the host OS kernel for lightweight, fast deployments, while VMs emulate full hardware environments for stronger isolation. The right choice depends on your requirements for speed, security, and compatibility.",
